ngthen: strengthen","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":291},{"base":"H1129","lemma":"בָּנָה","tr":"ba·nah","gloss":"to build","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":376},{"base":"H4026","lemma":"מִגְדָּל","tr":"mig·dal","gloss":"(Hananel) Tower","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":48},{"base":"H1817","lemma":"דָּל","tr":"dal","gloss":"door","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":88},{"base":"H6942","lemma":"קָדַשׁ","tr":"qa·dash","gloss":"to consecrate: consecate","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":171},{"base":"H0566","lemma":"אִמְרִי","tr":"im·ri","gloss":"Imri","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3968","lemma":"מֵאָה","tr":"me·ah","gloss":"(Tower of) the Hundred","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H8179","lemma":"שַׁ֫עַר","tr":"sha·ar","gloss":"gate","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":374},{"base":"H1195","lemma":"בַּעֲנָא","tr":"ba·a·na","gloss":"Baana","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4898","lemma":"מְשֵׁיזַבְאֵל","tr":"me·she·zav·el","gloss":"Meshezabel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NEH","chapter":12,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"over the Gate of Ephraim, the Jeshanah Gate, the Fish Gate, the Tower of Hananel, and the Tower of the Hundred, as far as the Sheep Gate. And they stopped at the Gate of the Guard.","from":1},{"book":"JER","chapter":31,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"“The days are coming,” declares the LORD, “when this city will be rebuilt for Me, from the tower of Hananel to the Corner Gate.","from":1},{"book":"JHN","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Now there is in Jerusalem near the Sheep Gate a pool with five covered colonnades, which in Hebrew is called Bethesda.","from":1},{"book":"2CH","chapter":33,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"After this, Manasseh rebuilt the outer wall of the City of David from west of Gihon in the valley to the entrance of the Fish Gate, and he brought it around the hill of Ophel and heightened it considerably. He also stationed military commanders in all the fortified cities of Judah.","from":3},{"book":"EZR","chapter":8,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"On the fourth day, in the house of our God, we weighed out the silver and gold and sacred articles into the hand of Meremoth son of Uriah, the priest. Eleazar son of Phinehas was with him, along with the Levites Jozabad son of Jeshua and Noadiah son of Binnui.","from":4},{"book":"NEH","chapter":12,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"over the Gate of Ephraim, the Jeshanah Gate, the Fish Gate, the Tower of Hananel, and the Tower of the Hundred, as far as the Sheep Gate. And they stopped at the Gate of the Guard.","from":3},{"book":"ZEC","chapter":14,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"All the land from Geba to Rimmon south of Jerusalem will be turned into a plain, but Jerusalem will be raised up and will remain in her place, from the Benjamin Gate to the site of the First Gate to the Corner Gate, and from the Tower of Hananel to the royal winepresses.","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":20,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Furthermore, the officers are to address the army, saying, “Has any man built a new house and not dedicated it? Let him return home, or he may die in battle and another man dedicate it.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"6-12":{"people":[{"id":"besodeiah-h1152","name":"Besodeiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned builder","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"joiada-h3111g","name":"Joiada","kind":"person","brief":"Returned builder","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"meshullam-h4918s","name":"Meshullam","kind":"person","brief":"Returned builder","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"paseah-h6454i","name":"Paseah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned builder","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"jadon-h3036","name":"Jadon","kind":"person","brief":"Returned builder","count":1,"firstV