assage":2,"uses":29},{"base":"H5393","lemma":"נִשְׁכָּה","tr":"nish·kah","gloss":"chamber","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4662","lemma":"מִפְקָד","tr":"miph·qad","gloss":"Muster (Gate)","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H0564","lemma":"אִמֵּר","tr":"im·mer","gloss":"Immer","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2CH","chapter":23,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So they seized Athaliah as she reached the entrance of the Horse Gate on the palace grounds, and there they put her to death.","from":28},{"book":"NEH","chapter":3,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"At the Sheep Gate, Eliashib the high priest and his fellow priests began rebuilding. They dedicated it and installed its doors. After building as far as the Tower of the Hundred and the Tower of Hananel, they dedicated the wall.","from":32},{"book":"2KI","chapter":11,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So they seized Athaliah as she reached the horsesʼ entrance to the palace grounds, and there she was put to death.","from":28},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the descendants of Immer, 1,052;","from":29},{"book":"EZR","chapter":10,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Shecaniah son of Jehiel, an Elamite, said to Ezra: “We have been unfaithful to our God by marrying foreign women from the people of the land, yet in spite of this, there is hope for Israel.","from":29},{"book":"NEH","chapter":3,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Next to them, Meremoth son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz, made repairs. Next to him, Meshullam son of Berechiah, the son of Meshezabel, made repairs; and next to him, Zadok son of Baana made repairs as well.","from":30},{"book":"NEH","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Next to them, Uzziel son of Harhaiah, one of the goldsmiths, made repairs. And next to him, Hananiah, one of the perfumers, made repairs. They fortified Jerusalem as far as the Broad Wall.","from":31},{"book":"NEH","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Next to them, Uzziel son of Harhaiah, one of the goldsmiths, made repairs. And next to him, Hananiah, one of the perfumers, made repairs. They fortified Jerusalem as far as the Broad Wall.","from":32}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}